  },
  "holistic_F_N": 2,
  "holistic_F_H": 2,
  "section_notes": "S1 mandates 24-hour reporting of confirmed incidents and 72-hour customer notice. S2 tests at 55°C with 5% regulator-review and 8% corrective-action thresholds but no sales stop, and provides per-model results to buyers. S3 requires new-unit shut-off from adoption and a 6-year retrofit; S4 requires built-in suppression or a validated equivalent at 36 months; S5 uses an 8/100k review trigger with regulator discretion on recalls and prompt notices, leaving S2 and S5 weakened."
 },
